{"task_id": "HumanEval/6", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef _calculate_max_depth_for_group(group_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum nesting depth within a single string of parentheses.\n    Non-parentheses characters are ignored, and current_depth can go negative for unbalanced groups.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_depth = 0\n    max_depth = 0\n    for char in group_string:\n        if char == '(':\n            current_depth += 1\n            max_depth = max(max_depth, current_depth)\n        elif char == ')':\n            current_depth -= 1\n    return max_depth\ndef parse_nested_parens(paren_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Input to this function is a string represented multiple groups for nested parentheses separated by spaces.\n    For each of the group, output the deepest level of nesting of parentheses.\n    E.g. (()()) has maximum two levels of nesting while ((())) has three.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(paren_string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    groups = paren_string.split(' ')\n    results: List[int] = []\n\n    for group in groups:\n        if group:  # Process only non-empty group strings.\n            results.append(_calculate_max_depth_for_group(group))\n\n    return results"}
