{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "class InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception raised for invalid input values.\"\"\"\n    pass\ndef largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the largest proper divisor of an integer n.\n    Raises TypeError if n is not an integer, or InvalidInputError if n <= 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n <= 1:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer greater than 1.\")\n\n    # Iterate from n // 2 down to 1; the largest proper divisor cannot be greater than n/2.\n    for i in range(n // 2, 0, -1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return i\n    \n    # If no other divisor is found (n is prime), 1 is the largest proper divisor.\n    return 1"}
