{"task_id": "HumanEval/26", "solution": "from typing import List\nfrom collections import Counter\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"\n    Custom exception for signaling invalid input data, inheriting from ValueError.\n    Raised when input is not a list of integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    pass\ndef remove_duplicates(numbers: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    From a list of integers, remove all elements that occur more than once,\n    preserving the order of the remaining elements.\n    Raises InvalidInputError if the input is not a list or contains non-integer elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    \n    if not all(isinstance(item, int) for item in numbers):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"All elements in the list must be integers.\")\n\n    counts = Counter(numbers)\n    result_list = []\n    for item in numbers:\n        if counts[item] == 1:\n            result_list.append(item)\n    return result_list"}
