{"task_id": "HumanEval/31", "solution": "import math\ndef is_prime(n):\n    \"\"\"Return true if a given number is prime, and false otherwise.\n    >>> is_prime(6)\n    False\n    >>> is_prime(101)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(11)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(13441)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(61)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(4)\n    False\n    >>> is_prime(1)\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1, 2):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/31", "solution": "def is_prime(n):\n    \"\"\"Return true if a given number is prime, and false otherwise.\n    >>> is_prime(6)\n    False\n    >>> is_prime(101)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(11)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(13441)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(61)\n    True\n    >>> is_prime(4)\n    False\n    >>> is_prime(1)\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n <= 3:  # 2 and 3 are prime.\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0 or n % 3 == 0:\n        return False\n    i = 5\n    while i * i <= n:\n        if n % i == 0 or n % (i + 2) == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 6\n    return True"}
