{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef sort_third(l: List) -> List:\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a new list where elements at indices\n    divisible by three are sorted, while other elements remain in their original positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(l, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    if not l:\n        return []\n\n    # Identify and extract elements at indices divisible by three.\n    third_elements = []\n    third_indices = []\n    for i, item in enumerate(l):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            third_elements.append(item)\n            third_indices.append(i)\n\n    # Sort the extracted elements.\n    try:\n        third_elements.sort()\n    except TypeError as e:\n        raise TypeError(f\"Elements in the list are not comparable: {e}\") from e\n\n    # Create a new list and place sorted elements back.\n    result_list = l[:]  # Shallow copy of the original list.\n    for i, sorted_val in zip(third_indices, third_elements):\n        result_list[i] = sorted_val\n\n    return result_list"}
