{"task_id": "HumanEval/34", "solution": "def unique(l: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a new list containing only the unique elements from the input list,\n    sorted in ascending order. Elements must be hashable and comparable.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> unique([5, 3, 5, 2, 3, 3, 9, 0, 123])\n        [0, 2, 3, 5, 9, 123]\n        >>> unique([])\n        []\n        >>> unique([1, 2, 3])\n        [1, 2, 3]\n        >>> unique([\"b\", \"a\", \"b\"])\n        ['a', 'b']\n    \"\"\"\n    # Use a set to efficiently remove duplicates.\n    unique_elements = set(l)\n\n    # Convert back to a list and sort.\n    sorted_unique_elements = sorted(list(unique_elements))\n\n    return sorted_unique_elements"}
