{"task_id": "HumanEval/38", "solution": "def decode_cyclic(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string that was cyclically encoded by `encode_cyclic`.\n    This reverses a right cyclic shift for blocks of `BLOCK_SIZE=3` only.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 's' must be a string.\")\n    if not s:\n        return \"\"\n\n    BLOCK_SIZE = 3 # This constant is used internally.\n\n    decoded_parts = []\n    for i in range(0, len(s), BLOCK_SIZE):\n        block = s[i : i + BLOCK_SIZE]\n        \n        # Only apply left cyclic shift if the block was originally shifted (i.e., len == BLOCK_SIZE).\n        if len(block) == BLOCK_SIZE:\n            # Perform a left cyclic shift to reverse the right shift: \"cab\" -> \"abc\".\n            decoded_block = block[1:] + block[0]\n        else:\n            # Blocks shorter than BLOCK_SIZE were not shifted by encode_cyclic.\n            decoded_block = block \n        \n        decoded_parts.append(decoded_block)\n\n    return \"\".join(decoded_parts)"}
