{"task_id": "HumanEval/41", "solution": "class CarRaceCollisionError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for all application-specific errors.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\nclass InvalidInputError(CarRaceCollisionError):\n    \"\"\"Represents errors due to invalid input parameters.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\ndef car_race_collision(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of collisions between two sets of `n` cars, one moving left-to-right and the other right-to-left.\n    Each car from one set collides with every car from the other set, resulting in `n*n` collisions.\n\n    Args:\n        n (int): The number of cars in each direction. Must be a non-negative integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The total number of collisions.\n\n    Raises:\n        InvalidInputError: If 'n' is not an integer or is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    return n * n"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/41", "solution": "from typing import Any\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid function inputs.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\nERROR_NON_INTEGER = \"Parameter '{param_name}' must be an integer.\"\nERROR_NEGATIVE_INTEGER = \"Parameter '{param_name}' must be a non-negative integer.\"\nclass InputValidator:\n    @staticmethod\n    def validate_positive_integer(value: Any, param_name: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Validates if a value is a non-negative integer. Raises InvalidInputError otherwise.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(value, int):\n            raise InvalidInputError(ERROR_NON_INTEGER.format(param_name=param_name))\n        if value < 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(ERROR_NEGATIVE_INTEGER.format(param_name=param_name))\n        return value\ndef car_race_collision(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Imagine a road that's a perfectly straight infinitely long line.\n    n cars are driving left to right; simultaneously, a different set of n cars\n    are driving right to left. The two sets of cars start out being very far from\n    each other. All cars move in the same speed. Two cars are said to collide\n    when a car that's moving left to right hits a car that's moving right to left.\n    However, the cars are infinitely sturdy and strong; as a result, they continue moving\n    in their trajectory as if they did not collide.\n\n    This function outputs the number of such collisions.\n    \"\"\"\n    validated_n = InputValidator.validate_positive_integer(n, \"n\")\n    return validated_n * validated_n"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/41", "solution": "def car_race_collision(n: int):\n    \"\"\"\n    Imagine a road that's a perfectly straight infinitely long line.\n    n cars are driving left to right;  simultaneously, a different set of n cars\n    are driving right to left.   The two sets of cars start out being very far from\n    each other.  All cars move in the same speed.  Two cars are said to collide\n    when a car that's moving left to right hits a car that's moving right to left.\n    However, the cars are infinitely sturdy and strong; as a result, they continue moving\n    in their trajectory as if they did not collide.\n\n    This function outputs the number of such collisions.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Number of cars 'n' cannot be negative.\")\n\n    return n * n"}
