{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "class InvalidBaseError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for errors in the input base.\"\"\"\n    pass\nclass InvalidNumberError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for errors in the input number (e.g., negative).\"\"\"\n    pass\nclass BaseConverter:\n    MIN_BASE = 2\n    MAX_BASE = 9\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _validate_base(base: int) -> None:\n        if not (BaseConverter.MIN_BASE <= base <= BaseConverter.MAX_BASE):\n            raise InvalidBaseError(f\"Base must be an integer between {BaseConverter.MIN_BASE} and {BaseConverter.MAX_BASE}.\")\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _validate_number(x: int) -> None:\n        if x < 0:\n            raise InvalidNumberError(\"Number to convert must be non-negative.\")\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _convert_recursive(number: int, base: int) -> str:\n        if number == 0:\n            return \"\"\n        remainder = number % base\n        quotient = number // base\n        return BaseConverter._convert_recursive(quotient, base) + str(remainder)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def change_base(x: int, base: int) -> str:\n        BaseConverter._validate_base(base)\n        BaseConverter._validate_number(x)\n\n        if x == 0:\n            return \"0\"\n\n        return BaseConverter._convert_recursive(x, base)\ndef change_base(x: int, base: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    Returns string representation after the conversion.\n    Base numbers are less than 10 (specifically 2-9).\n\n    Args:\n        x (int): The non-negative integer to convert.\n        base (int): The target base (must be between 2 and 9, inclusive).\n\n    Returns:\n        str: The string representation of x in the given base.\n\n    Raises:\n        InvalidBaseError: If the base is not between 2 and 9.\n        InvalidNumberError: If the number x is negative.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> change_base(8, 3)\n        '22'\n        >>> change_base(8, 2)\n        '1000'\n        >>> change_base(7, 2)\n        '111'\n    \"\"\"\n    return BaseConverter.change_base(x, base)"}
