{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "from typing import List\nclass Fib4Calculator:\n    \"\"\"Manages the state and logic for computing Fib4 numbers iteratively with memoization.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        # Initialize with base cases: fib4(0)=0, fib4(1)=0, fib4(2)=2, fib4(3)=0\n        self._memo: List[int] = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n        self._max_computed: int = 3\n\n    def get_fib4(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the n-th Fib4 number efficiently using an iterative approach and memoization.\n        Raises ValueError if n is negative.\n        \"\"\"\n        if n < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n        if n <= self._max_computed:\n            return self._memo[n]\n\n        # Compute values iteratively up to n and store them in _memo.\n        for i in range(self._max_computed + 1, n + 1):\n            next_fib4 = (\n                self._memo[i - 1] +\n                self._memo[i - 2] +\n                self._memo[i - 3] +\n                self._memo[i - 4]\n            )\n            self._memo.append(next_fib4)\n        \n        self._max_computed = n\n        return self._memo[n]\n_calculator = Fib4Calculator()\ndef fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Efficiently computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence using an iterative approach with memoization.\n    It follows the definition: fib4(0)=0, fib4(1)=0, fib4(2)=2, fib4(3)=0, and fib4(n)=fib4(n-1)+fib4(n-2)+fib4(n-3)+fib4(n-4) for n > 3.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _calculator.get_fib4(n)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence iteratively.\n    The sequence is defined with base cases and a recurrence relation for n > 3.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n        \n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the last four values: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    # a = fib4(i-4), b = fib4(i-3), c = fib4(i-2), d = fib4(i-1)\n    a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0 \n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = a + b + c + d\n        a, b, c, d = b, c, d, next_fib\n    \n    return d"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validates input `n`; it must be a non-negative integer.\n    # Computes fib4(n) iteratively for n > 3 using O(1) space, handling base cases directly.\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # a, b, c, d represent fib4(i-4), fib4(i-3), fib4(i-2), fib4(i-1) respectively.\n    a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        current_fib = a + b + c + d\n        a, b, c, d = b, c, d, current_fib\n    \n    return d"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize a list with the first four base Fib4 numbers: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3).\n    # This maintains a sliding window of the last four values needed for the recurrence.\n    current_fibs = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    # Iterate from the 4th element up to n, calculating each Fib4 number.\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = sum(current_fibs)\n        current_fibs.pop(0)  # Remove the oldest Fib4 number.\n        current_fibs.append(next_fib) # Add the newly computed Fib4 number.\n\n    return current_fibs[-1] # The last element in the list is fib4(n)."}
