{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "import collections\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception raised for invalid input values.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\nERROR_NEGATIVE_INPUT = \"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\"\ndef fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence. Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(ERROR_NEGATIVE_INPUT)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    last_four = collections.deque([0, 0, 2, 0], maxlen=4)\n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = sum(last_four)\n        last_four.append(next_fib)\n    \n    return last_four[-1]"}
