{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "def decode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes as input string encoded with encode_shift function. Returns decoded string.\n    Each lowercase English letter is shifted backward by 5 positions, wrapping around the alphabet.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    decoded_chars = []\n    SHIFT_AMOUNT = 5\n    ALPHABET_SIZE = 26\n    ORD_A = ord('a')\n    ORD_Z = ord('z')\n\n    for ch in s:\n        ord_ch = ord(ch)\n        if ORD_A <= ord_ch <= ORD_Z:\n            # Calculate 0-indexed position, apply negative shift, wrap around alphabet.\n            offset = ord_ch - ORD_A\n            shifted_offset = (offset - SHIFT_AMOUNT) % ALPHABET_SIZE\n            decoded_chars.append(chr(shifted_offset + ORD_A))\n        else:\n            decoded_chars.append(ch)\n\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)"}
