{"task_id": "HumanEval/64", "solution": "def vowels_count(s):\n    \"\"\"Counts vowels in a string, considering 'y' as a vowel only at the end.\n    Vowels are 'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u', case-insensitively.\n\n    Example:\n    >>> vowels_count(\"abcde\")\n    2\n    >>> vowels_count(\"ACEDY\")\n    3\n    >>> vowels_count(\"\")\n    0\n    >>> vowels_count(\"rhythm\")\n    1\n    >>> vowels_count(\"hello world\")\n    3\n    >>> vowels_count(\"yacht\")\n    1\n    >>> vowels_count(\"mystery\")\n    2\n    >>> vowels_count(\"symphony\")\n    2\n    >>> vowels_count(\"yyyyy\")\n    1\n    >>> vowels_count(\"supercalifragilisticexpialidocious\")\n    16\n    \"\"\"\n\n    standard_vowels = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n    y_vowel_char = 'y'\n\n    lower_s = s.lower()\n    vowel_count = 0\n\n    for char in lower_s:\n        if char in standard_vowels:\n            vowel_count += 1\n\n    if lower_s and lower_s[-1] == y_vowel_char:\n        vowel_count += 1\n\n    return vowel_count"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/64", "solution": "def vowels_count(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of vowels in the given string 's'.\n    Vowels are 'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'. 'y' is a vowel only when it is at the end of the word.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return 0\n\n    s_lower = s.lower()\n    count = 0\n    standard_vowels = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n\n    # Iterate through all characters except the last one\n    for char in s_lower[:-1]:\n        if char.isalpha() and char in standard_vowels:\n            count += 1\n\n    # Check the last character for standard vowels or conditional 'y'\n    last_char = s_lower[-1]\n    if last_char.isalpha():\n        if last_char in standard_vowels:\n            count += 1\n        elif last_char == 'y':\n            count += 1\n\n    return count"}
