{"task_id": "HumanEval/64", "solution": "def vowels_count(s):\n    \"\"\"Counts vowels in a string, including 'y' at the end of the string.\n    Vowels 'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u' are counted case-insensitively.\n\n    Examples:\n    >>> vowels_count(\"hello\")\n    2\n    >>> vowels_count(\"rhythm\")\n    1\n    >>> vowels_count(\"AEIOU\")\n    5\n    >>> vowels_count(\"happy\")\n    2\n    >>> vowels_count(\"yellow\")\n    2\n    >>> vowels_count(\"\")\n    0\n    >>> vowels_count(\"bcdfgh\")\n    0\n    >>> vowels_count(\"y\")\n    1\n    >>> vowels_count(\"Python\")\n    1\n    >>> vowels_count(\"syzygy\")\n    2\n    >>> vowels_count(\"aeiouy\")\n    6\n    >>> vowels_count(\"Hello, World!\")\n    3\n    >>> vowels_count(\"abcde\")\n    2\n    >>> vowels_count(\"ACEDY\")\n    3\n    \"\"\"\n    standard_vowels = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n    special_y_vowel = 'y'\n    count = 0\n    s_lower = s.lower()\n\n    for char in s_lower:\n        if char in standard_vowels:\n            count += 1\n\n    # Check if the string ends with 'y' and increment count if it does.\n    if s_lower.endswith(special_y_vowel):\n        count += 1\n\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "def circular_shift(x: int, shift: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Circular shift the digits of integer x to the right by 'shift' positions, returning the result as a string.\n    If 'shift' is greater than or equal to the number of digits, the digits are reversed.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_x = str(x)\n    n = len(s_x)\n\n    if shift >= n:\n        # If shift is too large or equal to number of digits, reverse the string.\n        return s_x[::-1]\n    else:\n        # Perform circular right shift using string slicing when shift is less than n.\n        effective_shift = shift\n        return s_x[-effective_shift:] + s_x[:-effective_shift]"}
