{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "def circular_shift(x: int, shift: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Circularly shifts the digits of integer x to the right.\n    If 'shift' exceeds the number of digits, the digits are reversed.\n    \"\"\"\n    is_negative = x < 0\n    s = str(abs(x))\n    n = len(s)\n\n    if shift > n:\n        result_s = s[::-1]  # Reverse digits if shift is greater than number of digits\n    else:\n        actual_shift = shift % n\n        # Perform circular right shift using string slicing\n        result_s = s[n - actual_shift:] + s[:n - actual_shift]\n\n    if is_negative and x != 0:\n        result_s = \"-\" + result_s  # Prepend sign if original number was negative and not zero\n    \n    return result_s"}
