{"task_id": "HumanEval/69", "solution": "from collections import Counter\ndef search(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the greatest integer X such that its frequency is greater than or equal to X.\n    Returns -1 if no such integer exists.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Calculate the frequency of each integer in the list.\n    frequencies = Counter(lst)\n\n    # Get unique numbers and sort them in descending order to find the greatest first.\n    unique_numbers = sorted(frequencies.keys(), reverse=True)\n\n    for num in unique_numbers:\n        # Check if the frequency of the number is greater than or equal to its value.\n        if frequencies[num] >= num:\n            return num # Return the first (greatest) number that satisfies the condition.\n\n    # If no such number is found after checking all unique numbers, return -1.\n    return -1"}
