{"task_id": "HumanEval/71", "solution": "import math\ndef triangle_area(a, b, c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given three side lengths, return the triangle's area rounded to 2 decimal points,\n    or -1.0 if the sides do not form a valid triangle.\n    \"\"\"\n    INVALID_TRIANGLE_RESULT = -1.0\n\n    # Check if all sides are positive and satisfy the triangle inequality theorem.\n    if not (a > 0 and b > 0 and c > 0):\n        return INVALID_TRIANGLE_RESULT\n    if not ((a + b > c) and (a + c > b) and (b + c > a)):\n        return INVALID_TRIANGLE_RESULT\n\n    # Calculate the semi-perimeter and then the area using Heron's formula.\n    s = (a + b + c) / 2\n    area_squared = s * (s - a) * (s - b) * (s - c)\n    # Ensure area_squared is non-negative due to potential floating point inaccuracies.\n    if area_squared < 0:\n        return 0.0\n\n    raw_area = math.sqrt(area_squared)\n\n    # Round the calculated area to two decimal places before returning.\n    rounded_area = round(raw_area, 2)\n    return rounded_area"}
