{"task_id": "HumanEval/73", "solution": "from typing import Any\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input. It stores a descriptive message.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\nclass InputValidator:\n    \"\"\"Utility for validating inputs. It checks if inputs are lists of integers.\"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def validate_integer_list(arr: Any) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates that the input is a list and all its elements are integers. Raises InvalidInputError on failure.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(arr, list):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n        for i, item in enumerate(arr):\n            if not isinstance(item, int):\n                raise InvalidInputError(f\"All elements in the list must be integers. Found non-integer at index {i}: {item}\")\ndef smallest_change(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array arr of integers, find the minimum number of elements that\n    need to be changed to make the array palindromic. A palindromic array is an array that\n    is read the same backwards and forwards. In one change, you can change one element to any other element.\n\n    For example:\n    smallest_change([1,2,3,5,4,7,9,6]) == 4\n    smallest_change([1, 2, 3, 4, 3, 2, 2]) == 1\n    smallest_change([1, 2, 3, 2, 1]) == 0\n    \"\"\"\n    InputValidator.validate_integer_list(arr)\n\n    changes_count = 0\n    left, right = 0, len(arr) - 1\n\n    while left < right:\n        if arr[left] != arr[right]:\n            changes_count += 1\n        left += 1\n        right -= 1\n\n    return changes_count"}
