{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "import re\ndef anti_shuffle(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes a string and returns an ordered version of it by sorting characters within each word.\n    The order of words and blank spaces in the sentence must be preserved.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 's' must be a string.\")\n\n    parts = re.split(r'(\\s+)', s)\n    \n    processed_parts = []\n    for part in parts:\n        if part.isspace() or not part:\n            processed_parts.append(part)\n        else:\n            processed_parts.append(\"\".join(sorted(part)))\n            \n    return \"\".join(processed_parts)"}
