{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "import re\ndef anti_shuffle(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes a string and returns an ordered version of it.\n    Characters within words are sorted based on their ASCII values, preserving original word order and spaces.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    # Split the string by one or more spaces, capturing the spaces themselves.\n    # This preserves the sequences of spaces for reassembly.\n    parts = re.split(r'(\\\\s+)', s)\n\n    result_parts = []\n    for part in parts:\n        if part:  # Process only non-empty string parts\n            if part.strip() == '':  # If the part consists entirely of spaces\n                result_parts.append(part)\n            else:  # Otherwise, it's a word (non-space characters)\n                result_parts.append(\"\".join(sorted(part)))\n            \n    return \"\".join(result_parts)"}
