{"task_id": "HumanEval/87", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple\nclass Coordinate:\n    def __init__(self, row: int, col: int):\n        self.row = row\n        self.col = col\n\n    def to_tuple(self) -> Tuple[int, int]:\n        return (self.row, self.col)\n\n    def __lt__(self, other: 'Coordinate') -> bool:\n        if self.row != other.row:\n            return self.row < other.row\n        return self.col > other.col\n\n    def __repr__(self) -> str:\n        return f\"Coordinate(row={self.row}, col={self.col})\"\ndef get_row(lst: List[List[int]], x: int) -> List[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds occurrences of integer x in a nested list and returns their\n    coordinates (row, column), sorted by row ascending, then column descending.\n    \"\"\"\n    found_coordinates: List[Coordinate] = []\n\n    for r_idx, row_list in enumerate(lst):\n        for c_idx, element in enumerate(row_list):\n            if element == x:\n                found_coordinates.append(Coordinate(r_idx, c_idx))\n\n    found_coordinates.sort()\n\n    return [coord.to_tuple() for coord in found_coordinates]"}
