{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "def sort_array(array: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a copy of the array: ascending if the sum of first and last elements is odd,\n    descending if the sum is even. Handles empty or single-element arrays by returning a copy.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array) < 2:\n        return list(array)\n\n    array_copy = list(array)\n    sum_first_last = array[0] + array[-1]\n\n    if sum_first_last % 2 == 1:\n        array_copy.sort(reverse=False)\n    else:\n        array_copy.sort(reverse=True)\n\n    return array_copy"}
