{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "def encrypt(s):\n    \"\"\"Create a function encrypt that takes a string as an argument and\n    returns a string encrypted with the alphabet being rotated. \n    The alphabet should be rotated in a manner such that the letters \n    shift down by two multiplied to two places.\n    For example:\n    encrypt('hi') returns 'lm'\n    encrypt('asdfghjkl') returns 'ewhjklnop'\n    encrypt('gf') returns 'kj'\n    encrypt('et') returns 'ix'\n    \"\"\"\n    SHIFT_VALUE = 4\n    encrypted_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            base = ord('a')\n            offset = ord(char) - base\n            rotated_offset = (offset + SHIFT_VALUE) % 26\n            encrypted_chars.append(chr(base + rotated_offset))\n        elif 'A' <= char <= 'Z':\n            base = ord('A')\n            offset = ord(char) - base\n            rotated_offset = (offset + SHIFT_VALUE) % 26\n            encrypted_chars.append(chr(base + rotated_offset))\n        else:\n            encrypted_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(encrypted_chars)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "_SHIFT_AMOUNT = 4\n_ALPHABET_LOWER = \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\"\n_ALPHABET_UPPER = \"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ\"\ndef encrypt(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Encrypts a string using a rotational cipher with a shift of 4.\n    Non-alphabetic characters are preserved; case is maintained.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    encrypted_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        if char.islower():\n            idx = _ALPHABET_LOWER.find(char)\n            new_idx = (idx + _SHIFT_AMOUNT) % len(_ALPHABET_LOWER)\n            encrypted_chars.append(_ALPHABET_LOWER[new_idx])\n        elif char.isupper():\n            idx = _ALPHABET_UPPER.find(char)\n            new_idx = (idx + _SHIFT_AMOUNT) % len(_ALPHABET_UPPER)\n            encrypted_chars.append(_ALPHABET_UPPER[new_idx])\n        else:\n            encrypted_chars.append(char)\n    \n    return \"\".join(encrypted_chars)"}
