{"task_id": "HumanEval/91", "solution": "import re\ndef is_bored(S):\n    \"\"\"\n    You'll be given a string of words, and your task is to count the number\n    of boredoms. A boredom is a sentence that starts with the word \"I\".\n    Sentences are delimited by '.', '?' or '!'.\n   \n    For example:\n    >>> is_bored(\"Hello world\")\n    0\n    >>> is_bored(\"The sky is blue. The sun is shining. I love this weather\")\n    1\n    \"\"\"\n    SENTENCE_DELIMITERS_PATTERN = r'(?<=[.?!])\\s*'\n\n    def _split_sentences(text: str) -> list:\n        \"\"\"\n        Splits the input text into a list of sentences.\n        Filters out any empty strings and strips whitespace.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not text:\n            return []\n        \n        sentences = re.split(SENTENCE_DELIMITERS_PATTERN, text)\n        # Filter out any empty strings that might result from splitting\n        # and clean up leading/trailing whitespace for each sentence\n        return [s.strip() for s in sentences if s.strip()]\n\n    def _is_bored_sentence(sentence: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if a single sentence starts with the word \"I\" (case-insensitive,\n        ignoring leading whitespace).\n        \"\"\"\n        cleaned_sentence_start = sentence.strip().lower()\n        # Check for \"I\" as a standalone word or \"I \" followed by other words\n        return cleaned_sentence_start == \"i\" or cleaned_sentence_start.startswith(\"i \")\n\n    sentences = _split_sentences(S)\n    boredom_count = 0\n    for sentence in sentences:\n        if _is_bored_sentence(sentence):\n            boredom_count += 1\n    return boredom_count"}
