{"task_id": "HumanEval/107", "solution": "def even_odd_palindrome(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, return a tuple that has the number of even and odd\n    integer palindromes that fall within the range(1, n), inclusive.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or not (1 <= n <= 1000):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer between 1 and 1000, inclusive.\")\n\n    def is_palindrome(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if an integer is a palindrome by comparing its string representation with its reverse.\"\"\"\n        return str(num) == str(num)[::-1]\n\n    def is_even(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if an integer is even using the modulo operator.\"\"\"\n        return num % 2 == 0\n\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if is_palindrome(i):\n            if is_even(i):\n                even_count += 1\n            else:\n                odd_count += 1\n\n    return (even_count, odd_count)"}
