{"task_id": "HumanEval/107", "solution": "def even_odd_palindrome(n):\n    \"\"\"Counts even and odd integer palindromes within the range [1, n].\n    Validates input `n` to be an integer between 1 and 1000.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or not (1 <= n <= 1000):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer between 1 and 1000, inclusive.\")\n\n    def is_palindrome_number(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a given integer is a palindrome by comparing its string representation.\"\"\"\n        s_num = str(num)\n        return s_num == s_num[::-1]\n\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n\n    for num in range(1, n + 1):\n        if is_palindrome_number(num):\n            if num % 2 == 0:\n                even_count += 1\n            else:\n                odd_count += 1\n\n    return (even_count, odd_count)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/108", "solution": "def count_nums(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts numbers in an array whose custom digit sum is greater than zero.\n    For negative numbers, the first digit after the minus sign is treated as negative.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_digit_sum(num: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the sum of digits for an integer according to custom rules.\n        The first digit of a negative number is parsed as negative.\n        \"\"\"\n        if num == 0:\n            return 0\n\n        s_num = str(num)\n        digit_sum = 0\n\n        if s_num[0] == '-':\n            # The first digit (e.g., -1 from -123) is considered negative.\n            # This handles single-digit negative numbers like -5 as well.\n            digit_sum += int(s_num[0] + s_num[1])\n            start_index = 2\n        else:\n            # For non-negative numbers, all digits are positive.\n            start_index = 0\n\n        for digit_char in s_num[start_index:]:\n            digit_sum += int(digit_char)\n\n        return digit_sum\n\n    count = 0\n    for number in arr:\n        # Increment count if the calculated digit sum for the current number is positive.\n        if _calculate_digit_sum(number) > 0:\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
