{"task_id": "HumanEval/109", "solution": "def move_one_ball(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if an array can be sorted in non-decreasing order by right shifts.\n    The input array `arr` is guaranteed to have unique elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # An empty or single-element array is considered sorted.\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    descent_count = 0\n    \n    # Count the number of descents (where arr[i] > arr[i+1]).\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        if arr[i] > arr[i+1]:\n            descent_count += 1\n            # If more than one descent is found, it cannot be sorted by rotation.\n            if descent_count > 1:\n                return False\n\n    # If no descents, the array is already sorted.\n    if descent_count == 0:\n        return True\n    # If exactly one descent, check the wrap-around condition (last < first).\n    # This indicates a single valid rotation point.\n    else: # descent_count == 1\n        return arr[n-1] < arr[0]"}
