{"task_id": "HumanEval/134", "solution": "def check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(txt):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the last character of a string is an alphabetical character\n    and is not part of a word, as defined by space separation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not txt:\n        return False\n\n    last_char = txt[-1]\n\n    if not last_char.isalpha():\n        return False\n\n    if len(txt) == 1:\n        # A single alphabetical character is considered a word itself.\n        return False\n    else:\n        char_before_last = txt[-2]\n        if char_before_last == ' ':\n            # The last character is a standalone word, hence \"not part of a word\".\n            return True\n        else:\n            # The last character is part of a multi-character word.\n            return False"}
